(Description)
Given an array of strings strs, group the anagrams together. You can return the answer in any order.

--- Solution ---
class Solution {
    public List<List<String>> groupAnagrams(String[] strs) {
        Map<String, List<String>> map = new HashMap<>();

        for (String str : strs) {
            int[] count = new int[26];

            for (char c : str.toCharArray()) {
                count[c - 'a']++;
            }

            String key = Arrays.toString(count);

            map.putIfAbsent(key, new ArrayList<>());
            map.get(key).add(str);
        }

        return new ArrayList<>(map.values());
    }
}

--- Approach ---
(An anagram is a word formed by rearranging the letters of a different word)

Because anagrams share same numbers of letters to form the word
=> Key point of this algorithm is tracking the numbers of the given word.
  To track the numbers, it used int array using its index as a pointer to the character.
  For example, if a character was found from the given word, it counts 1 at the position of 0. //Becasue index 0 points to lowercase 'a'.

If anagrams were searched properly, in next they should be distinguished at the distinct exact List.
=> At this moment, HashSet could figure out the solution.
  It stores a distinct List with the key that is the count.
  Then, all of the words could be distinguished easily to ask is the combination of letters existed before, or am I first?
